WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.360
- State-of-the-art bag sorting,
automated security lanes,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.390
and something I rarely
experience at an airport,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.503
it's really quiet.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.217
SFO just won WSJ's Best airport of 2022

00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:17.160
and I'm here to see why.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.320
So I toured the airport's newest space,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.530
the $2.5 billion Harvey Milk Terminal One

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:26.250
to test out the amenities and
go and check out the logistics

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.040
that helped SFO beat
its closest competition,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.824
Minneapolis and Atlanta.

00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:33.060
We'll start behind the scenes.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.410
- Let's do it.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.080
- [Adam] This is Ivar Satero,
he's the airport director here

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.450
and my tour guide for the day.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.650
- Okay, come on through.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.180
- Thank you.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.160
So we are in the bag system

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.960
underneath at Harvey Milk Terminal one.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.030
- This is the zone between

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.680
when you drop your bag off at check in

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.530
and when your bag gets on whatever plane

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:53.580
you're taking out of SFO.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.480
- Exactly.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.460
- This tote-based baggage
system is the first

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.310
of its kind in the US,
and SFO says it's helping

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.410
to smooth the airport's operations.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.910
Basically, every bag is paired

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.013
with one of these white bins or totes.

00:01:05.013 --> 00:01:07.382
Each with our own unique
identifying number,

00:01:07.382 --> 00:01:09.360
which allows the bag and the tote

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.640
to be more easily tracked
along its journey.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.120
- Here we have the totes coming out

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.912
and the bags are dropping into the totes.

00:01:17.912 --> 00:01:22.020
- [Adam] This system can move
up to 450 bags per minute.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.220
That's more than twice that

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.080
of a traditional conveyor system.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.520
And SFO says it gets backed up less often

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.423
than other baggage systems too

00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:31.440
- For travelers I mean, it just, you know,

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.480
increases the chances that your bag

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.050
is going to get to and
from the plane as you hope.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:38.250
- [Adam] I sat down with my colleague,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.797
WSJ columnist Dawn Gilbertson,

00:01:39.797 --> 00:01:40.920
who spends a lot of time

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.200
thinking about the traveler experience

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.760
- After the nightmare summer

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:49.590
a lot of travelers had with
lost luggage, it's a bonus.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.320
- But equally as important
as how an airport routes bags

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.940
is how it moves people.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.070
Terminal one's layout helps with that.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.500
Just look at its eight
automated security lanes.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.800
They are both wider and longer
than others in the airport.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.480
- And you can see there's this island here

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.475
and so you can really just take your tray

00:02:05.475 --> 00:02:06.837
and move over to the island,

00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:09.840
and give someone else an
opportunity to see their bag.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.837
- [Adam] But if that's not
enough space to tie your shoes,

00:02:11.837 --> 00:02:14.728
SFO has this 11,000 square foot space

00:02:14.728 --> 00:02:16.770
it calls the recompose area.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.470
That's just a fancy way
of saying post-security.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.560
SFO sees this space as a place
where travelers can reset,

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.740
dare I say relax, before
venturing to their gates.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:28.380
And soon any traveler could
enter through terminal one

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.904
because SFO is working to connect

00:02:29.904 --> 00:02:32.130
all terminals post-security

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.050
- We're excited about
finishing the last phase

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.238
of Harvey Milk Terminal One,
which well then complete

00:02:36.238 --> 00:02:39.810
the horseshoe of our terminal complex.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:40.867
- That means travelers connecting here

00:02:40.867 --> 00:02:44.533
won't have to exit and go back
through another checkpoint

00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:46.770
just to make their next flight.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:48.984
Right now though, terminal
one is only connected

00:02:48.984 --> 00:02:51.212
to part of the international terminal.

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:54.990
Those logistical upgrades are
aimed at making travel easier.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.880
But to score high in our rankings,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.090
SFO also had to provide the
amenities travelers want.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.990
Sure, there's free wifi
and local restaurants

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.768
which you can find in any airport,

00:03:03.768 --> 00:03:06.030
but there's something else.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.313
One amenity just about
everybody can enjoy.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.313
Just listen.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.450
SFO has what it calls the
Quiet Airport Initiative.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.760
The airport urges travelers
to use headphones,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.145
and it strictly limits the
number of overhead announcements

00:03:20.145 --> 00:03:22.530
broadcast to the entire terminal.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.450
Something we noticed while we were there.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.020
- [PA Announcer] Zoe Moss,
courtesy telephone please.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.370
- That's only the second
announcement I've heard

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.990
the entire time I've been here.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.480
- And one of the most
popular amenities at SFO

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.220
is its water refill stations.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.250
Travelers go through 32,500 gallons

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.939
of water here each month.

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:43.470
They can fill up with hot,
cold, or room temperature water.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.303
What's next?

00:03:44.303 --> 00:03:46.710
Are you gonna start
putting some soda machines

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:47.910
or anything else in here?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.408
- More people now want Perrier
or their seltzer water.

00:03:50.408 --> 00:03:51.596
- Sparkling water, yeah.

00:03:51.596 --> 00:03:52.429
That can be next.
- So sparking water

00:03:52.429 --> 00:03:54.930
is something we're thinking about, so yes.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.763
- Wow.

00:03:55.763 --> 00:03:59.013
Okay, well, sparkling water
coming to SFO soon maybe.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.980
All of these amenities
have helped the airport

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.051
receive high marks in
customer satisfaction.

00:04:04.051 --> 00:04:06.300
It placed second in a J.D. Power survey

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.475
which weighs heavily in the WSJ rankings.

00:04:08.475 --> 00:04:10.907
- J.D. Power looks at
six different factors,

00:04:10.907 --> 00:04:13.260
and it's everything
from check-in, you know,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.660
through security, through
shopping and dining

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.770
and baggage claim.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.760
- We're talking about the things

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.396
that travelers really interact with

00:04:19.396 --> 00:04:20.550
once they get to the air.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.383
- Exactly, yes.

00:04:21.383 --> 00:04:23.220
I mean, what a lot of us
remember about an airport

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.410
besides whether our
flight was on-time or not.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.835
- That's right, because those amenities

00:04:26.835 --> 00:04:29.610
are only really enjoyable to travelers

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.040
who aren't angry about delayed travel.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.290
But at SFO, delays aren't common.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.656
It's among the airports with the highest

00:04:35.656 --> 00:04:38.070
on-time arrival and departures rate.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.695
- Their on-time arrivals and
departures were both above 80%,

00:04:40.695 --> 00:04:42.420
and it wasn't that long ago.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.010
In fact, it was 2019 in our
last survey where it was 72%.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.022
That's, you know, that's a
big improvement for people.

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:52.230
- [Adam] Still, those numbers
don't tell the whole story.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:54.180
At SFO, travel has yet to return

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.890
to what it was before the pandemic.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.780
Both passenger and flight volumes

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.120
are still down more than 25%

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.070
according to airport statistics.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.908
- The two big international
markets out of San Francisco

00:05:04.908 --> 00:05:09.390
pre pandemic were London and Hong Kong,

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.820
and Hong Kong only just reopened recently,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.410
you know, to people without a quarantine.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.750
So, you know, that means
less congestion here.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.340
It helps the on-time performance for sure.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.450
- Is there any reason to believe

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:22.620
that once those numbers boost
back up to a hundred percent

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.310
that SFO might have trouble
keeping their high ranks

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:27.720
in on-time arrivals and departures?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.910
- Yeah, that's the million dollar question

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.070
- [Adam] But Satero says he isn't worried.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.020
- We have a very busy bank in the morning.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.200
Actually our morning bank is
busier than it was pre COVID.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.810
And so I think really the factors

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:44.550
are around larger aircraft
and higher load factors

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.870
is really what's helping us,

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.120
and I think that's sustainable.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.198
- [Adam] San Francisco's top
ranking could be confusing

00:05:50.198 --> 00:05:53.010
for those just looking at price, however.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.511
- Obviously, what travelers
really care the most about

00:05:55.511 --> 00:05:58.890
are ticket prices and San
Francisco didn't fare so well

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.120
in the value category.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:01.950
- [Adam] Compared to nearby
San Jose and Oakland,

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:05.034
SFO's average ticket prices are higher.

00:06:05.034 --> 00:06:09.938
27% more than San Jose
and 39% more than Oakland.

00:06:09.938 --> 00:06:13.440
SFO says this is due in
part to lack of competition

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.570
for travel to some destinations.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.579
- There's just markets
that are captured markets

00:06:17.579 --> 00:06:19.560
that there isn't...

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.080
The competition in that
airfares will be higher

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.076
- [Adam] Still, the combination
of more reliable flights

00:06:24.076 --> 00:06:26.850
and top-notch amenities helped SFO

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.119
overcome its high prices
to give it WSJ's top spot.

00:06:30.119 --> 00:06:32.820
And the airport isn't done upgrading.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.400
- We've been opening in phases
over the last couple years

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.041
as we've completed
sections of the terminal.

00:06:38.041 --> 00:06:43.041
We've brought them online and
now we're about 75% complete.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.870
- [Adam] Of course, SFO
isn't the only airport

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.520
updating its space.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.140
- Everybody's always
trying to up their game

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.280
'cause there's so much competition

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.570
especially in this region.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.938
- So what's it gonna
take for San Francisco

00:06:52.938 --> 00:06:55.043
to be top of the list again next year?

00:06:55.043 --> 00:06:56.877
- They've just gotta
keep the momentum going

00:06:56.877 --> 00:07:00.294
and make sure the process is seamless,

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:04.577
and hopefully the
congestion stays in check.

00:07:04.577 --> 00:07:07.577
(soft bright music)

